  "verbalization": "Ceftazidime is implicated in the pathogenesis of peritonitis through a series of interconnected indications. The drug is linked to endometritis, a condition that can lead to peritonitis, and endometritis is associated with cefoxitin and cilastatin, both of which are also linked to peritonitis. This suggests a potential pathway where ceftazidime may contribute to the development of peritonitis via the induction of endometritis, which in turn could predispose to peritonitis. The evidence is supported by the shared indication of peritonitis across multiple pathways, indicating a possible role of ceftazidime in the development of this condition through a chain of bacterial infections or inflammatory responses. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of ceftazidime in the progression of peritonitis, particularly through its involvement in endometritis, which may serve as a critical intermediate step in the disease process.",
